language.name = English
mod.cogwork.name = Cogwork
mod.cogwork.description = Tubes, engines and machines that automate mining, crafting and leveling land. Cuboid loaders keep them working with nobody near.
mod.cogwork.authors = Zorro909
tab.cogwork.cogwork = Cogwork

item.cogwork.wooden_cog = Wooden Cog
item.cogwork.stone_cog = Stone Cog
item.cogwork.iron_cog = Iron Cog
item.cogwork.gold_cog = Gold Cog
item.cogwork.diamond_cog = Diamond Cog
item.cogwork.tuning_wrench = Tuning Wrench
item.cogwork.tuning_wrench.tooltip = Use on a directing tube to change its output, on an engine to turn it.

block.cogwork.stone_tube = Stone Tube
block.cogwork.stone_tube.tooltip = Carries items to the tubes and machines it touches.
block.cogwork.timber_tube = Timber Extraction Tube
block.cogwork.timber_tube.tooltip = Pulls items out of the chests and machines it touches when an engine drives it: one item a stroke with a spring engine, eight with an ember engine. Two of them don't join.
block.cogwork.gilded_tube = Gilded Tube
block.cogwork.gilded_tube.tooltip = Speeds up the items going through it.
block.cogwork.sorting_tube = Sorting Tube
block.cogwork.sorting_tube.tooltip = Every side has its own color, on its arm and beside its row of samples. Click a row with items to set its samples; the items stay with you. Sends each item out of the side whose row holds a sample of it, or else out of a side with an empty row.
block.cogwork.directing_tube = Directing Tube
block.cogwork.directing_tube.tooltip = Sends everything out of one side. Change it with a tuning wrench.
block.cogwork.void_tube = Void Tube
block.cogwork.void_tube.tooltip = Destroys every item that reaches it.

block.cogwork.torque_shaft = Torque Shaft
block.cogwork.torque_shaft.tooltip = Carries energy between engines and machines, and joins any mod's cables.
block.cogwork.wooden_axle = Wooden Axle
block.cogwork.wooden_axle.tooltip = A cheap shaft of wood: carries energy between water wheels, engines and machines as a torque shaft does.
block.cogwork.water_wheel = Water Wheel
block.cogwork.water_wheel.tooltip = A wheel three blocks across. Makes 12 energy a tick while flowing water, not a still source, runs under it, and pushes it out of its axle into the block it was placed against. Place it one block above a stream.

block.cogwork.spring_engine = Spring Engine
block.cogwork.spring_engine.tooltip = Wind it with an empty hand: each turn of its crank winds in 200 energy, up to 10,000. It runs down at 10 a tick into the block its trunk points at; a redstone signal holds it still.
block.cogwork.ember_engine = Ember Engine
block.cogwork.ember_engine.tooltip = Burns fuel, but not lava, for four times the energy of a spring engine. Stops to cool down when its energy has nowhere to go.

block.cogwork.excavator = Gantry Excavator
block.cogwork.excavator.tooltip = The biggest quarry. Digs out the area marked out by survey markers next to it, else the area of a frame it is placed against, else the area behind it, down as deep as the world allows; blocks more than 64 below it cost more energy. It runs only on more energy per tick than its standby, which grows with the length of its sides; what comes in beyond that sets how fast it digs.
block.cogwork.gantry_frame = Gantry Frame
block.cogwork.timber_quarry = Timber Quarry
block.cogwork.timber_quarry.tooltip = A small, slow quarry of wood and string. Builds a frame of 1 log and 1 string a block from its frame slots, up to 7 by 7 inside (5 by 5 without markers), then digs 16 layers below itself with the drill bit in its bit slot. What its bit can't break stays standing. Standby 4 energy a tick.
block.cogwork.lashed_frame = Lashed Frame
block.cogwork.iron_quarry = Iron Quarry
block.cogwork.iron_quarry.tooltip = A sturdier quarry of iron. Builds a frame of 1 iron ingot a block from its frame slots, up to 17 by 17 inside (9 by 9 without markers), then digs 64 layers below itself with the iron or steel drill bit in its bit slot, bringing up a quarter more Ore Rubble. Standby grows with its sides, as the Gantry's.
block.cogwork.iron_frame = Iron Frame
block.cogwork.steel_excavator = Steel Excavator
block.cogwork.steel_excavator.tooltip = A big quarry of steel. Builds a frame of steel lattice from its frame slots, 1 steel ingot for every 4 frame blocks, up to 63 by 63 inside (9 by 9 without markers), then digs down to the world's lowest layer for excavators with the steel or diamond-tipped drill bit in its bit slot, bringing up half as much Ore Rubble again. Standby grows with its sides, as the Gantry's.
block.cogwork.steel_frame = Steel Frame
item.cogwork.stone_bit = Stone Drill Bit
item.cogwork.stone_bit.tooltip = For the Timber Quarry: breaks what a stone pickaxe breaks, up to 12 energy a tick, for 400 blocks.
item.cogwork.iron_bit = Iron Drill Bit
item.cogwork.iron_bit.tooltip = For the Timber Quarry (up to 18 energy a tick) and the Iron Quarry (up to 60): breaks what an iron pickaxe breaks, gold and diamond too, for 2,000 blocks.
item.cogwork.steel_bit = Steel Drill Bit
item.cogwork.steel_bit.tooltip = For the Iron Quarry (up to 90 energy a tick) and the Steel Excavator (up to 120): breaks what a diamond pickaxe breaks, for 8,000 blocks.
item.cogwork.diamond_bit = Diamond-Tipped Drill Bit
item.cogwork.diamond_bit.tooltip = For the Steel Excavator (up to 160 energy a tick): breaks what a diamond pickaxe breaks, for 40,000 blocks.
block.cogwork.assembly_bench = Assembly Bench
block.cogwork.assembly_bench.tooltip = Click its pattern cells with items to lay out a crafting recipe; the items stay with you. Tubes then fill the cells with stacks of their ghosts, and with engine power it makes the recipe again and again, one item of each cell a craft. A timber tube takes the results out.
block.cogwork.leveler = Leveler
block.cogwork.leveler.tooltip = Makes the area behind it, or the one marked out by survey markers next to it, flat at its height: clears up to 16 blocks above and fills holes up to 4 deep with whole blocks from its stock.
block.cogwork.survey_marker = Survey Marker
block.cogwork.survey_marker.tooltip = Place up to three more along two straight lines to mark a rectangle, then put an excavator or a leveler next to one. Use one to see the area; a marker without one puffs.
block.cogwork.cuboid_loader = Cuboid Loader
block.cogwork.cuboid_loader.tooltip = Keeps its own cube (16 by 16 by 16 blocks) loaded with nobody near, so machines there go on working. Its screen switches to keeping everything running there, mobs and growing plants too.
block.cogwork.ultra_cuboid_loader = Ultra Cuboid Loader
block.cogwork.ultra_cuboid_loader.tooltip = Keeps the 7 by 7 cubes around it loaded at its height, three each way. Its screen switches between keeping only machines running there and everything.
item.cogwork.cuboid_lens = Cuboid Lens
item.cogwork.cuboid_lens.tooltip = Held, outlines every cube Cogwork keeps loaded: cyan where a loader keeps machines running, green where it keeps everything, orange around a working excavator or leveler.

block.cogwork.rubble = Rubble
block.cogwork.rubble.tooltip = Broken stone, as quarries bring it up. Sifts into sand and gravel, and now and then something better.
item.cogwork.ore_rubble = Ore Rubble
item.cogwork.ore_rubble.tooltip = {if:cogwork:ore.named==1}{lang:cogwork.metal.iron}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==2}{lang:cogwork.metal.gold}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==3}{lang:cogwork.metal.copper}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==4}{lang:cogwork.metal.tin}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==5}{lang:cogwork.metal.silver}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==6}{lang:cogwork.metal.lead}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==7}{lang:cogwork.metal.zinc}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==8}{lang:cogwork.metal.nickel}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==9}{lang:cogwork.metal.aluminum}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==10}{lang:cogwork.metal.uranium}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==11}{lang:cogwork.metal.osmium}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==12}{lang:cogwork.metal.platinum}{/if}{if:cogwork:ore.named==0}{lang:cogwork.metal.other}{/if}, {if:cogwork:grade==0}{lang:cogwork.grade.poor}{/if}{if:cogwork:grade==1}{lang:cogwork.grade.common}{/if}{if:cogwork:grade==2}{lang:cogwork.grade.rich}{/if}{if:cogwork:grade==3}{lang:cogwork.grade.pure}{/if}
    {on_key:!core:sneak}{lang:tooltip.more}{/on_key}{on_key:core:sneak}Grinds into its metal's raw ore at a millstone or a grinding mill: one of Poor, two of Rich. Processing raises the grade.{/on_key}
block.cogwork.millstone = Millstone
block.cogwork.millstone.tooltip = Grinds Ore Rubble into raw ore by hand. Use it with a water bucket, sand and Ore Rubble, then with an empty hand to turn it: six turns grind one. Sneak with an empty hand to take out what it holds.
block.cogwork.sieve = Sieve
block.cogwork.sieve.tooltip = Sifts Rubble and slag by hand. Use it with Rubble or slag to put one on its mesh, then shake it four times with an empty hand.
block.cogwork.shaker_screen = Shaker Screen
block.cogwork.shaker_screen.tooltip = Sifts Rubble and slag with engine energy, as the sieve does: 800 energy at up to 20 a tick, two seconds each. They come in by tube; what it sifts out leaves by its front.
block.cogwork.grinding_mill = Grinding Mill
block.cogwork.grinding_mill.tooltip = Grinds Ore Rubble into raw ore with engine energy, as the millstone does: 800 energy at up to 40 a tick. Takes water by liquid tube (125 mB a grind) and sand by tube (4 grinds a sand); the raw ore leaves by its front.
block.cogwork.washer = Washer
block.cogwork.washer.tooltip = Washes Poor Ore Rubble into Common with engine energy: 400 energy at up to 30 a tick and 250 mB of water by liquid tube a wash. Ore Rubble comes in by tube and leaves by its front; Ore Rubble washed already goes straight through.
block.cogwork.flotation_cell = Flotation Cell
block.cogwork.flotation_cell.tooltip = Floats Common Ore Rubble into Rich with engine energy: 1,200 energy at up to 40 a tick, 500 mB of water and 50 mB of creosote a float, leaving 250 mB of muddy water. Water comes in by liquid tube; creosote it draws from a liquid tube, tank or coke oven drain beside it; muddy water leaves by its back. Ore Rubble comes in by tube and leaves by its front; other grades go straight through.
block.cogwork.clarifier = Clarifier
block.cogwork.clarifier.tooltip = Settles muddy water back into water, slowly and with no energy: 5 mB a tick, 900 mB of water from every 1,000, and a one in ten chance of a clay ball. Muddy water comes in by liquid tube; water leaves by its front, clay by its other sides.
block.cogwork.muddy_water = Muddy Water
item.cogwork.muddy_water_bucket = Muddy Water Bucket
block.cogwork.core_drill = Core Drill
block.cogwork.core_drill.tooltip = Tells what ore lies below it. Turn it with an empty hand: each turn drills 8 layers deeper, and after 16 turns it says in chat how many blocks of each ore lie in the 16 by 16 square around it, in bands of 16 layers down to 128 below.
block.cogwork.hand_bellows = Hand Bellows
block.cogwork.hand_bellows.tooltip = Place it against a furnace and pump it with an empty hand: the furnace cooks twice as fast for a minute.
block.cogwork.driven_bellows = Driven Bellows
block.cogwork.driven_bellows.tooltip = Blows into the furnace it is placed against while an engine feeds it 20 energy a tick, steadily: the furnace cooks twice as fast. Against a blast furnace it gives the draft it smelts by, for 80 a tick.

block.cogwork.coke_oven = Coke Oven
block.cogwork.coke_oven.tooltip = The door of a coke oven: a 3 by 3 by 3 box of coke oven bricks behind it, hollow in the middle. Cooks coal into coke, eight at a time in 45 seconds, with no energy: 250 mB of creosote a coal and a sulfur every eight. Coal comes in by tube; coke and sulfur leave by its front.
block.cogwork.coke_oven_bricks = Coke Oven Bricks
block.cogwork.coke_oven_bricks.tooltip = The walls of a coke oven.
block.cogwork.coke_oven_drain = Coke Oven Drain
block.cogwork.coke_oven_drain.tooltip = Takes the place of a brick anywhere in a coke oven's walls and lets its creosote out into liquid tubes. A bucket fills from it.
block.cogwork.creosote = Creosote
item.cogwork.creosote_bucket = Creosote Bucket
item.cogwork.coke = Coke
item.cogwork.coke.tooltip = Coal baked in a coke oven: burns twice as long as coal, and is what a blast furnace smelts steel with.
item.cogwork.sulfur = Sulfur
item.cogwork.sulfur.tooltip = Comes out of a coke oven, one for every eight coal.
block.cogwork.blast_furnace = Blast Furnace
block.cogwork.blast_furnace.tooltip = The tap hole of a blast furnace: a box of fire bricks 3 by 3 and 4 high behind and above it, hollow up the middle above the bottom. A driven bellows blowing into its bottom layer gives it the draft, at 80 energy a tick; then an iron ingot and a coke smelt in 20 seconds into a steel bloom and slag.
block.cogwork.fire_bricks = Fire Bricks
block.cogwork.fire_bricks.tooltip = The walls of a blast furnace.
item.cogwork.steel_bloom = Steel Bloom
item.cogwork.steel_bloom.tooltip = A spongy lump of steel from the blast furnace. Lay it on a forge anvil and strike it five times with a forge hammer for a steel ingot.
item.cogwork.slag = Slag
item.cogwork.slag.tooltip = What a blast furnace leaves of the ore. Sifts into gravel, and now and then a Poor iron Ore Rubble.
item.cogwork.steel_ingot = Steel Ingot
block.cogwork.steel_block = Block of Steel
block.cogwork.forge_anvil = Forge Anvil
block.cogwork.forge_anvil.tooltip = Use it with a steel bloom to lay it on the face, then strike it five times with a forge hammer: the steel ingot pops out on top. An empty hand takes the bloom back.
item.cogwork.forge_hammer = Forge Hammer
item.cogwork.forge_hammer.tooltip = Strikes steel blooms on a forge anvil, wearing a little each time: enough for fifty ingots.

block.cogwork.firebox = Firebox
block.cogwork.firebox.tooltip = Burns fuel under a boiler placed on it, only while the boiler can boil: any fuel item from a tube or by hand, lava buckets too, and lava by liquid tube. Its fuel lasts half as long as in an ember engine.
block.cogwork.boiler = Boiler
block.cogwork.boiler.tooltip = Stands on a firebox and boils 20 mB of water into 20 mB of steam a tick while it burns. Water comes in by liquid tube on any side; steam goes out of its top. Holds 8,000 mB of water and 4,000 of steam.
block.cogwork.steam = Steam
block.cogwork.steam_engine = Steam Engine
block.cogwork.steam_engine.tooltip = Runs on 20 mB of steam a tick by liquid tube for 160 energy a tick, pushed out of both ends of its flywheel's axle and into torque shafts and wooden axles beside it.
block.cogwork.trip_hammer = Trip Hammer
block.cogwork.trip_hammer.tooltip = Forges steel blooms into steel ingots with a steam-lifted hammer: five strikes a bloom, 10 mB of steam by liquid tube a strike. Blooms come in by tube; ingots leave by its front.

block.cogwork.oil = Oil
item.cogwork.oil_bucket = Oil Bucket
block.cogwork.oily_dirt = Oil-Soaked Dirt
block.cogwork.oily_dirt.tooltip = Lies around a seep of oil, above a field of it deep below.
block.cogwork.oil_sand = Oil Sand
block.cogwork.oil_sand.tooltip = Lies around a seep of oil, above a field of it deep below.
block.cogwork.pump = Pump
block.cogwork.pump.tooltip = Bores straight down with engine power until it reaches a liquid, then pumps a bucket of it a second, the farthest from its hose first. Liquid tubes take the liquid away; what it bores through goes to the chests and tubes beside it.
block.cogwork.pump_hose = Pump Hose
block.cogwork.liquid_tube = Liquid Tube
block.cogwork.liquid_tube.tooltip = Holds a bucket of one liquid and passes it on to the liquid tubes, tanks and pumps it touches, from the fuller to the emptier. You can see how full it is.
block.cogwork.timber_liquid_tube = Timber Liquid Tube
block.cogwork.timber_liquid_tube.tooltip = A liquid tube with a small pump in it. When an engine drives it, it pulls liquid out of the tanks it touches and pushes it up to 16 blocks up the liquid tubes beside it: a bucket for 1,000 energy, a bucket every 5 seconds with a spring engine.
block.cogwork.liquid_tank = Liquid Tank
block.cogwork.liquid_tank.tooltip = Holds 16 buckets of one liquid. Tanks next to each other become one tank when together they make a box of up to 3 by 3 and 6 high. A bucket fills it or is filled from it.
block.cogwork.oil_engine_controller = Oil Engine Controller
block.cogwork.oil_engine_controller.tooltip = The front of an oil engine: a 3 by 3 by 3 cube behind it, a combustion chamber in its middle, intakes and drives anywhere on its shell but this face and the top, casing all round. Built, it burns oil with water for 600 energy a tick, about 4 hours on a medium oil field.
block.cogwork.oil_engine_casing = Oil Engine Casing
block.cogwork.oil_engine_casing.tooltip = The shell of an oil engine: every block of it not taken by its controller, intakes and drives.
block.cogwork.combustion_chamber = Combustion Chamber
block.cogwork.combustion_chamber.tooltip = The heart of an oil engine, in the middle of its cube.
block.cogwork.oil_intake = Oil Engine Intake
block.cogwork.oil_intake.tooltip = Where an oil engine takes in oil, or water for vapor, from liquid tubes or buckets: one liquid at a time, so give each its own. Goes anywhere on its shell but the front and the top.
block.cogwork.oil_engine_drive = Oil Engine Drive
block.cogwork.oil_engine_drive.tooltip = Where an oil engine's energy leaves it, up to 1,000 a tick: into the blocks it faces and the torque shafts it joins. Goes anywhere on its shell but the front and the top.
